        "uuid": "d0218832_c73ddde7",
        "filename": "board/samus/gesture.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-14T22:18:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, this is on purpose. if you look at a plot of sum_z, it is clear why. before the first tap, the data is very near 0. but after a tap, the delta_z slowly decreases back down to 0 because it is still vibrating a little. So, the outer window after the last tap has a much higher delta_z than the outer window before the first tap. It is not symmetric.",
      "parentUuid": "901b9006_e61cb092",
      "revId": "42a577fe90a2dc992130c32a9a4daa31248561d1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
